AB  - The concept of symmorphosis postulates a matching of structural capacity to functional demand within a defined physiological system, regardless of endurance exercise training status. Whether this concept applies to oxygen (O-2) supply and demand during maximal skeletal muscle O-2 consumption ((V) over dot(O2max)) in humans is unclear. Therefore, in vitro skeletal muscle mitochondrial. (V) over dot(O2max) ((Mito) V over dot(O2max), mitochondrial respiration of fibres biopsied from vastus lateralis) was comparedwith in vivo skeletalmuscle. (V) over dot(O2max) during single leg knee extensor exercise ((KE) (V) over dot(O2max), direct Fick by femoral arterial and venous blood samples andDoppler ultrasound blood flow measurements) and whole-body. (V) over dot(O2max) during cycling ((Body) (V) over dot(O2max), indirect calorimetry) in 10 endurance exercise-trained and 10 untrained young males. In untrained subjects, during KE exercise, maximal O2 supply (KE (Q) over dot O-2max) exceeded (462 +/- 37 ml kg(-1) min(-1), P < 0.05) and (KE) (V) over dot(O2max) matched (340 +/- 22 ml kg(-1) min(-1), P > 0.05) (Mito) (V) over dot(O2max) (364 +/- 16 ml kg(-1) min(-1)). Conversely, in trained subjects, both (KE) (Q) over dot O-2max (557 +/- 35 ml kg(-1) min(-1)) and (KE) (V) over dot(O2max) (458 +/- 24 ml kg(-1) min(-1)) fell far short of (Mito) (V) over dot(O2max) (743 +/- 35 ml kg(-1) min(-1), P < 0.05). Although (Mito) (V) over dot(O2max) was related to (KE) (V) over dot(O2max) (r = 0.69, P < 0.05) and (Body) (V) over dot(O2max) (r = 0.91, P < 0.05) in untrained subjects, these variables were entirely unrelated in trained subjects. Therefore, in untrained subjects, (V) over dot(O2max) is limited by mitochondrial O-2 demand, with evidence of adequate O-2 supply, whereas, in trained subjects, an exercise training-induced mitochondrial reserve results in skeletal muscle. (V) over dot(O2max) being markedly limited by O-2 supply. Taken together, these in vivo and in vitro measures reveal clearly differing limitations and excesses at (V) over dot(O2max) in untrained and trained humans and challenge the concept of symmorphosis as it applies to O-2 supply and demand in humans.
